WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.560
- And I would notice over the years,

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:03.040
no matter where I was working,

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:04.700
whatever market I worked in

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:06.850
and whatever station I worked for,

00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:07.683
there was always that,

00:00:07.683 --> 00:00:09.480
"Don't make the sponsors,

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:11.702
the people paying for
the commercials mad."

00:00:11.702 --> 00:00:14.285
(upbeat music)

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:27.370
- I'm Dave Rubin and joining me today

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:29.790
is a former television news journalist

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:32.540
and now candidate for governor

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:34.970
of the great state of Arizona, Kari Lake.

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:36.010
Welcome to the Rubin Report.

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:36.843
- Hi, Dave.

00:00:36.843 --> 00:00:37.676
Thank you for having me.

00:00:37.676 --> 00:00:39.800
I'm so excited to be here.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:42.340
- Kari, I have to start very obviously

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:45.700
my audience is gonna hear
former television journalists.

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:46.750
They're gonna freak out

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:49.380
because they don't like journalists.

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:51.950
Am I allowed to call
you a former journalist

00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:53.140
without using air quotes?

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:55.140
Because, journalists these days,

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:56.302
I think you get it.

00:00:56.302 --> 00:00:59.950
- Well, I came up through
the old school of journalism

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:02.500
where you told both sides of the story.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:03.600
If there were three sides,

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:04.900
you told all three sides

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:06.490
and you kept your opinions out.

00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:09.050
And that's why I walked
away from my career.

00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:11.200
I started in journalism 30 years ago

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:12.380
and that's how you did it.

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:15.110
And now we've increasingly seeing

00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:17.110
journalists moving on, out,

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:19.420
being replaced with propagandas.

00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:21.551
And I was at the top of my game,

00:01:21.551 --> 00:01:23.630
number one in ratings for pretty much

00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:25.750
my entire time covering Arizona.

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:28.720
Most recently, 22 years
at the Fox affiliate,

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:31.790
number one, that whole
time making a fortune,

00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:32.970
had a pretty good life.

00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:34.080
And then COVID struck

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:36.510
and I realized there are no good guys

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:38.240
in the corporate media.

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:39.650
If there were good guys,

00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:40.970
they would've covered ivermectin,

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:42.970
told us about hydroxychloroquine.

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:44.810
They would've been
honest about the election

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:46.580
and the corruption involved in that.

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:48.223
And I just...

00:01:48.223 --> 00:01:50.207
I looked up in my career and said,

00:01:50.207 --> 00:01:52.180
"Oh my gosh, I can't do this anymore.

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:53.590
I don't wanna be part of this."

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:56.050
It was getting increasingly more difficult

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:58.390
to be honest with the people of Arizona.

00:01:58.390 --> 00:02:00.780
And if I couldn't speak 100% truth,

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:03.500
I didn't wanna be part
of it, so I walked away.

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:06.370
I do think there are some
good journalists out there.

00:02:06.370 --> 00:02:08.150
The ones you're seeing
on the corporate media,

00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:11.710
unfortunately, are mainly
propagandist today.

00:02:11.710 --> 00:02:13.180
- Do you remember a moment

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:15.040
that you started getting
an inkling of all that?

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:16.320
Did it really start with COVID

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:18.440
or I suspect in 22 years,

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:20.440
you probably saw some other hints

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:23.175
leading to where we got to today?

00:02:23.175 --> 00:02:26.070
- The news has increasingly been moving

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:27.360
toward the left, obviously,

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:28.920
over the past many decades.

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:30.490
And I just always felt like,

00:02:30.490 --> 00:02:31.470
well, as long as I keep

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:32.870
what comes outta my mouth

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:34.070
and when I'm being a journalist,

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:36.820
I can keep that on the straight and narrow

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:38.720
and make sure that I'm being fair.

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:41.710
I can't always be responsible
for everybody else

00:02:41.710 --> 00:02:42.960
that works in the industry,

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:44.880
but I know I can be for myself.

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:47.880
And I really truly felt
that I could do that

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:50.100
for the most part, almost all the time.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:53.330
And so that's what kept
me going in my career.

00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:55.839
There's always that, I guess,

00:02:55.839 --> 00:02:58.556
it would be the law of
television broadcasting

00:02:58.556 --> 00:03:01.360
and really any news entity,

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:03.320
they wanna protect their sponsors.

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:05.050
And I would notice over the years,

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:06.430
no matter where I was working,

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:08.070
whatever market I worked in,

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:10.230
and whatever station I worked for,

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:11.063
there was always that,

00:03:11.063 --> 00:03:12.880
"Don't make the sponsors,

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:15.300
the people paying for
the commercials mad."

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:19.590
For example, if a big car company in town,

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:21.160
if there was a scandal somehow,

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:23.480
it was always pulling teeth

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:26.120
to get management to wanna
cover something like that.

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:27.940
They would maybe cover it if they had to,

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:31.050
but it would be a short
20-second version of the story

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:33.960
rather than covering it ad
nauseam like they would,

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:36.050
if it was somebody who wasn't a sponsor.

00:03:36.050 --> 00:03:38.360
And looking back, you see things like that

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:40.300
and you go, "Wow, that's
a really dangerous thing,"

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:42.590
because we saw this during COVID.

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:45.580
These news outlets took
hundreds of millions of dollars

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:48.330
from Fauci and Big Pharma.

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:50.550
And you almost saw it happening.

00:03:50.550 --> 00:03:51.599
You almost saw it like this,

00:03:51.599 --> 00:03:53.700
like somebody flipped a switch,

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.130
and they all started talking

00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:58.200
so positively about the vaccines.

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:00.830
And there was no critical coverage of it.

00:04:00.830 --> 00:04:03.330
Now I'm not trying to be
judgmental on a vaccine,

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:05.800
but it is our responsibility
as journalists

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:06.960
to put out the truth

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:08.910
and not to tout a product,

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:11.350
and not to refuse to cover

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:12.507
the dangerous side effects

00:04:12.507 --> 00:04:14.090
because the people are counting

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:16.040
on truth from journalism,

00:04:16.040 --> 00:04:17.370
at least they used to.

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:20.240
And so when you see all these TV people

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:23.141
and newspaper people putting
out only the positives

00:04:23.141 --> 00:04:25.390
and trying to shame
people into getting shots,

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:27.080
but not covering the true side effects.

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:28.630
And there are some very dangerous

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:30.430
side effects with these shots,

00:04:30.430 --> 00:04:31.870
I believe they have blood on their hands.

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:34.230
And I'm so thankful that I got out

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:35.980
before that business started up,

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:38.650
because I was watching
that happen with horror,

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:40.670
knowing specifically people

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:42.500
who had terrible side effects

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:46.670
and actually blamed relatives
deaths on those shots,

00:04:46.670 --> 00:04:48.600
and then sitting there
and watching journalists

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:50.550
tout them and pump them up

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:51.820
like they were the greatest thing.

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:55.950
I think it's disgraceful
and hinging on criminal.

00:04:55.950 --> 00:04:58.040
- Are you amazed how
they can sort of do it

00:04:58.040 --> 00:04:59.380
right in front of our eyes?

00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:01.100
I don't know if you've
seen that compilation

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:02.520
that was going viral for a while.

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:04.200
We've shown it a couple times on my show,

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:07.270
where they show you all the
outros to the commercials,

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:09.130
the intros and outros to the commercials

00:05:09.130 --> 00:05:10.120
on mainstream media,

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:12.607
CNN, CBS, Morning News,
et cetera, et cetera,

00:05:12.607 --> 00:05:14.640
"Brought to you by Pfizer."

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:16.380
The same people who are telling you

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:18.530
how wonderful Pfizer is the entire time.

00:05:18.530 --> 00:05:19.890
I thought at one time we were supposed

00:05:19.890 --> 00:05:21.910
to be skeptical about this stuff?

00:05:21.910 --> 00:05:23.550
- I saw that, I saw that compilation.

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:24.650
At first, I didn't believe it

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:26.293
'cause sometimes you see
these compilations and you go,

00:05:26.293 --> 00:05:28.038
that can't be true.
- Yep.

00:05:28.038 --> 00:05:29.580
- I was just watching.

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:32.840
I was leaving North Carolina a day ago

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:34.770
and I was watching one
of the major networks,

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:35.603
Morning Show,

00:05:35.603 --> 00:05:36.436
and they were talking

00:05:36.436 --> 00:05:38.420
about the teen suicide rate

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:40.580
and teen mental illness and all of that.

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:42.600
And they did a whole segment on it

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:43.830
and what to look out for.

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:46.020
They didn't talk about
what caused a lot of it,

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:49.630
which was these draconian shutdowns

00:05:49.630 --> 00:05:51.150
and lockdowns and quarantines,

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:53.810
unnecessarily the
masking of our teenagers,

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:55.540
which wasn't needed and caused

00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:58.220
all kinds of mental problems
and sending them home.

00:05:58.220 --> 00:05:59.640
They didn't talk about that.

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:01.410
They just talked about how we've got teens

00:06:01.410 --> 00:06:03.280
with a bunch of emotional issues now

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:06.110
and right out of it was an ad for,

00:06:06.110 --> 00:06:07.880
I forget which big pharma,

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:11.060
about a drug for depression

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:12.890
and suicide and all of that.
- [Dave] Rexulti.

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:14.000
- And I'm like, wow,

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:15.880
it's so obvious once your eyes

00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:17.170
are woken up to to it.

00:06:17.170 --> 00:06:19.370
But some people just
aren't awake yet, Dave.

00:06:20.550 --> 00:06:21.960
- Some people are not awake.

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:23.240
There's a lot of woke people,

00:06:23.240 --> 00:06:24.650
just not a lot of awake people.

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:26.220
That seems to be the problem.

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:29.670
You did an event about two
weeks ago here in Florida,

00:06:29.670 --> 00:06:30.540
I was gonna try to get there

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:31.440
and then something popped up.

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:32.700
But you were at Mar-a-Lago

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:35.183
with a certain orange man.

00:06:35.183 --> 00:06:38.040
We'll play quick 10-second clip,

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:39.673
here is what he had to say about you.

00:06:39.673 --> 00:06:41.555
- But I will say that I think

00:06:41.555 --> 00:06:42.543
that's gonna be one of the great things

00:06:42.543 --> 00:06:44.920
that I've done endorsing a woman

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:46.294
and helping her get elected.

00:06:46.294 --> 00:06:48.279
And I think she'll go down
as the greatest governor.

00:06:48.279 --> 00:06:51.029
(crowd cheering)

00:06:52.450 --> 00:06:54.190
- All right, so it looks like you've got,

00:06:54.190 --> 00:06:55.023
or not looks like,

00:06:55.023 --> 00:06:56.280
you've got the endorsement of Trump.

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:57.803
You've done events with him.

00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:00.820
How does that feel relative

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:02.820
to getting into politics
for the first time

00:07:02.820 --> 00:07:04.570
and just the general state of craziness

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:07.037
on the circus that is
our political machine.

00:07:07.037 --> 00:07:11.240
- Well, that sound bite
you just played was just...

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:12.960
It felt really good to hear that

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:15.720
because I do plan on
being the best governor,

00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:17.549
best governor Arizona's ever seen.

00:07:17.549 --> 00:07:19.290
Probably probably be the first governor

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:22.250
Arizona's ever seen that truly was in it

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:24.130
for the right reasons to represent

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:25.530
the great people of this state.

00:07:25.530 --> 00:07:29.060
So when he said one of his
greatest accomplishments

00:07:29.060 --> 00:07:31.260
will be to help get me elected.

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:32.628
And he knows I'll become

00:07:32.628 --> 00:07:35.793
one of the greatest
governors in the country

00:07:35.793 --> 00:07:37.180
that made me feel really good

00:07:37.180 --> 00:07:38.390
because I'm in this for the right.

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:41.700
Trust me, there's no
reason you'd wanna get

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:45.870
into the corrupt world
of the Swampy politics,

00:07:45.870 --> 00:07:47.650
unless you're doing it
for the right reason.

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:49.160
I'm not in it for the fame.

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:50.200
There's no money in it.

00:07:50.200 --> 00:07:51.340
If you're an honest person

00:07:51.340 --> 00:07:53.920
and you're not trying
to build the taxpayers

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:55.140
out of their money.

00:07:55.140 --> 00:07:57.350
I'm just doing this
because I love Arizona.

00:07:57.350 --> 00:07:58.660
And I looked at the field

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:00.710
of people who was running, Dave,

00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:03.363
and I believe this is the
last election in this country.

00:08:03.363 --> 00:08:04.610
If we don't get it right,

00:08:04.610 --> 00:08:06.480
ad we don't get some America First people

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:07.313
in there running,

00:08:07.313 --> 00:08:09.170
some honest citizen politicians,

00:08:09.170 --> 00:08:10.003
I don't know that we'll have

00:08:10.003 --> 00:08:12.130
a country beyond this election.

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:14.160
So I looked at the
field of who was running

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:17.780
and it's the typical
RINO career politician,

00:08:17.780 --> 00:08:21.320
somebody who's run are, lost 20 years ago.

00:08:21.320 --> 00:08:23.960
We have somebody who's run before

00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:25.800
and run against Katie Hobbs,

00:08:25.800 --> 00:08:27.560
who's gonna be the Democrat socialist

00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:29.030
that we end up running against.

00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:31.650
And he already lost to
her a few years ago.

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:34.150
So I looked at the field
of Republicans running

00:08:34.150 --> 00:08:36.330
and I said, not a single one of them

00:08:36.330 --> 00:08:38.080
can get us past the finish line.

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:40.260
And if we lose this election

00:08:40.260 --> 00:08:41.500
and we get a Katie Hobbs,

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:43.610
who is a socialist Democrat,

00:08:43.610 --> 00:08:45.100
we will lose Arizona.

00:08:45.100 --> 00:08:46.650
And we cannot, as a country,

00:08:46.650 --> 00:08:49.060
afford to lose another border state.

00:08:49.060 --> 00:08:51.260
We'll be stuck with just Texas

00:08:51.260 --> 00:08:52.470
holding the line for us.

00:08:52.470 --> 00:08:56.110
And we need to get strong governors

00:08:56.110 --> 00:08:57.800
in these border states

00:08:57.800 --> 00:08:59.570
to hold the line for America.

00:08:59.570 --> 00:09:01.450
We are about to lose our country.

00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:03.920
If we don't have fair
elections and honest elections,

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:06.100
and we don't have a border,

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:07.490
then we do not have a country.

00:09:07.490 --> 00:09:08.770
So this race is critical

00:09:08.770 --> 00:09:10.350
and that's why I'm in it.

00:09:10.350 --> 00:09:12.030
- So I wanna jump back to the border stuff

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:12.863
in just a sec,

00:09:12.863 --> 00:09:14.040
but can you talk a little bit

00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:16.770
about what generally
is going on in Arizona?

00:09:16.770 --> 00:09:18.607
I think most people think of Arizona

00:09:18.607 --> 00:09:19.440
and they're like,

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:21.030
"No, no, it should be a red state.

00:09:21.030 --> 00:09:23.070
It seems like it's a red state,

00:09:23.070 --> 00:09:25.860
but it doesn't fully
seem to be a red state."

00:09:25.860 --> 00:09:28.150
It really, as you're
saying, could go either way.

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:29.340
It's a little hard to understand

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:32.230
what the electorate is
really made up of there

00:09:32.230 --> 00:09:33.510
or where they're really going.

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:34.870
- Well, let me tell you Arizona

00:09:34.870 --> 00:09:36.990
is as red as my shirt, okay?

00:09:36.990 --> 00:09:38.320
It's a red state.

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:42.210
But when we have corrupt
elections that are stolen,

00:09:42.210 --> 00:09:44.290
where we have mail-in ballots

00:09:44.290 --> 00:09:46.320
being sent out to people
who don't even live here

00:09:46.320 --> 00:09:47.720
and filled out and sent in

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:49.630
and we have ballot trafficking

00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:52.740
and we have more voters

00:09:52.740 --> 00:09:55.260
than even registered voters voting.

00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:57.290
Then we're gonna have a corrupt election

00:09:57.290 --> 00:09:59.100
that makes it look like
we aren't a red state.

00:09:59.100 --> 00:10:01.230
And that's why it is imperative

00:10:01.230 --> 00:10:03.580
that we get to the
bottom of this election.

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:06.340
And we do not allow another
election to be stolen.

00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:09.010
It's not about Republican,
Democrat, independent.

00:10:09.010 --> 00:10:11.150
It's about having honest elections

